# N4 (LMX_semantics.ru.md #dynamic: the admission turns the correspondence into one physical map for reading, writing,
# @ and publication): @x in S is the cell of x in D, not a cell of S. put adds 5 through it, so D\x becomes 15; the
# bare x is never written, so its clean working value is not published over 15. k publishes 0 into its own slot of D,
# and the pad of D keeps 1. Entry 7.
fn: put (@: p int) int
    \p: \p + 5
return: 0
S:
    int: x
    int: k put(@x)
end: S
D:
    int: k 9
    int: pad 1
    int: x 10
end: D
call: S D
int: r 81
if: D\x = 15 && D\k = 0 && D\pad = 1
    r: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
